@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: a game that stops around turn 45 with a failed draw is a bug to reproduce, then a resolver to fix — not a new mode
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no turn counter, draw resolver, or stop
'   condition exists under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate
'   the owning engine module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   forfeit must stay a different mapping _spec/_plans/forfeit-as-loss.puml
'   export is how the fixture is captured _spec/_plans/game-export-localstorage.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "game stopped? Turn 45 draw failed?" is an INCIDENT, not a feature. Two
' observations, both uncertain:
'   the game STOPPED (UI hung, rules ended, or persist refused)
'   a DRAW at about TURN 45 FAILED (claim rejected, detector threw, or
'     the stop was mislabelled as a draw)
'
' Treat those as hypotheses until a dump exists. Shipping a "turn 45 always
' draws" patch without a fixture is how a second stop gets invented.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   fifty-move, repetition, stalemate, or a house draw clock
'   whether 45 is exact or "late game"
'   host vs guest vs tutorial
'
' Do not fold this into forfeit-as-loss. A failed draw that becomes a forfeit
' is a third bug.
title PLANNED — reproduce the turn-45 stop;\ndo not invent a draw rule to paper over it

component "turn ~45" as T45 <<app>>
component "draw claim or detector" as DRAW <<app>>
component "**the game stops**\nhung UI · ended rules · persist fail" as STOP <<error>>
component "a dump from localStorage" as DUMP <<app>>
component "draw resolver with a fixture" as FIX <<app>>
component "**a new draw rule**\nwith no failing case" as FAKE <<error>>

T45 ARROW_MAIN DRAW
DRAW ARROW_ERROR STOP
STOP ARROW_OPTIONAL DUMP : export the blob
DUMP ARROW_MAIN FIX
STOP ARROW_ERROR FAKE : if patched from the title
FAKE ARROW_ERROR DRAW

note bottom of STOP
  **Stop is three independent failures: a hung
  interface, a terminal rules state, or a refused
  persist.** Classify which failure a captured
  dump shows before selecting a module to patch.
end note

note bottom of DRAW
  **A failed draw is not a refused claim: a legal
  draw that throws is a resolver defect.** A claim
  the rules reject is operating as designed, and
  the fixture has to distinguish those cases.
end note

note right of FAKE
  **Do not introduce a house draw at turn forty-
  five, because the reported number is a clue
  rather than a specification.** A synthetic rule
  at that turn would conceal the genuine detector.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Capture one blob.** Use game-export-localstorage.puml (or a debug copy
  of the key) at the moment of the stop. Record turn number, whose clock,
  last move, and the exact on-screen copy.
  --
  **2. Classify before coding.** Hung UI, rules terminal state, or persist
  exception. Only the second belongs in the draw resolver; the first is a
  journey bug, the third is the export/persist path.
  ==
  **3. Fix with that fixture as a test.** Replay the dump; the draw either
  completes to a draw outcome or is rejected without stopping the game. Do
  not map it to a forfeit.
  --
  **Left open**: which draw law is in play; whether tutorials share the
  resolver; whether 45 is reproducible or a coincidence.
end legend
@enduml
